ve difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$? Express your answer in simplest form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b66c68e10386bc998e7bacea58bdd9adda26162dc40dd86f60c5b08dfe974b9e"},"seconds":39.64594507217407,"seed":432704308696085403,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{11}{8},\\frac{6}{16}\\right\\}$, we first need to compare these fractions. To do this effectively, we can convert each fraction to its decimal form or find a common denominator, but in this case, finding a common denominator might be the more straightforward approach for comparison.\n\nFirst, let's simplify or rewrite each fraction if possible:\n- $\\frac{3}{7}$ is already in simplest form.\n- $\\frac{4}{3}$ is already in simplest form.\n- $\\frac{11}{8}$ is already in simplest form.\n- $\\frac{6}{16}$ can be simplified to $\\frac{3}{8}$ by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2.\n\nSo, we have the set $\\left\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{11}{8}, \\frac{3}{8}\\right\\}$.\n\nNext, we find a common denominator for these fractions. The least common multiple of 7, 3, 8, and 8 is 168. We convert each fraction to have this common denominator:\n- $\\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{3 \\times 24}{7 \\times 24} = \\frac{72}{168}$\n- $\\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{4 \\times 56}{3 \\times 56} = \\frac{224}{168}$\n- $\\frac{11}{8} = \\frac{11 \\times 21}{8 \\times 21} = \\frac{231}{168}$\n- $\\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{3 \\times 21}{8 \\times 21} = \\frac{63}{168}$\n\nNow, we can easily compare these fractions:\n- $\\frac{63}{168}$ (which is $\\frac{3}{8}$)\n- $\\frac{72}{168}$ (which is $\\frac{3}{7}$)\n- $\\frac{224}{168}$ (which is $\\frac{4}{3}$)\n- $\\frac{231}{168}$ (which is $\\frac{11}{8}$)\n\nFrom these, we see that the smallest fraction is $\\frac{3}{8}$ and the largest fraction is $\\frac{11}{8}$. The positive difference between these two is:\n\\[\n\\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
